    [Ops][Misc][Refactor] Refactor sampling primitives and clean up MRv1 dependencies (#19393)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    This PR refactors the 310P sampling primitives by moving them from the
    MRv1-only `vllm_ascend._310p.sample` package to the MRv2 worker under
    `vllm_ascend._310p.worker.v2.sample_utils`. This enables the eventual
    deletion of the MRv1-only sampling package without affecting the MRv2
    path. Additionally, it removes the obsolete `patch_rejection_sampler.py`
    patch, relocates greedy rejection sampling helpers to
    `vllm_ascend.worker.v2.sample.rejection_greedy`, and eliminates the
    `HardwareCapability.NPU_TOP_K_TOP_P` capability along with
    `_apply_top_k_top_p_torch_npu` since the sort-based PyTorch fallback is
    consistently faster and is now the sole implementation.
    
    Feedback: In `vllm_ascend/_310p/worker/v2/sample_utils.py`, clearing the
    generator cache on every call to `_prepare_cpu_generators_310p` evicts
    generators for temporarily absent requests, causing them to be re-seeded
    and generate repetitive tokens. It is recommended to remove the
    `.clear()` call and only update the cache.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No. This is an internal refactoring of sampling utilities and worker
    paths.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    The changes were verified by updating and running existing unit tests,
    such as `tests/ut/_310p/sample/test_sampler_310.py`,
    `tests/ut/device/test_hardware_profile.py`, and
    `tests/ut/sample/test_sampler.py`.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: I reviewed whether this change
    involves
    boundary conditions (e.g. empty input, single/zero element, min/max
    values,
    off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow). Where applicable,
    I
    added unit tests covering these edge cases in `tests/ut/` or
    `tests/e2e/`.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: If this PR fixes a bug, I added a regression
    test
      that would fail without the fix.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: I covered abnormal paths
    (exceptions,
    timeouts, out-of-range, division by zero) in addition to the happy path.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior
    and are
      not written merely to satisfy CI.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: If this PR touches a performance-sensitive
    path,
      I attached benchmark results and added performance regression tests.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
